course: dictionary
lesson: 11134
title: Wide: far across, or covering a lot
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Wide means far from one side to the other. When you read a sentence, look for clues about how big something is across. «Walk wide around swings» tells you to keep a big gap between you and the swing, so wide means far away from the side.
explain: Wide also tells how far across something is, as in «3 feet wide». In «Darwin's bark spider spins webs across rivers up to about 25 metres wide», wide tells you how far the web reaches from one bank to the other. Ask yourself: is the sentence telling me a distance across?
explain: Wide can mean covering many things, as in «a wide choice». It can also be an adverb that means fully or far, as in «wide open» and «wide awake». Try the swap test: put a simple word in place of wide, such as big, open or fully, and check that the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Wide means far from one side to the other.
fact: Wide tells how far across something is, such as a road, a river or a door.
fact: Wide can also mean covering many things, as in «a wide choice».
fact: «Wide awake» means fully awake, and «wide open» means fully open.
fact: Width is the noun: it means how wide something is.
exercise: «A moving swing is heavy and fast, so walk wide around swings.» What does walk wide mean here? | Walk very fast | Walk in a circle close by | Walk on the swings | *Keep a big gap from the swings
exercise: «A squid has eight arms plus two longer tentacles with suckers only on their wide tips.» In «wide tips», what does wide mean? | *Broad, far across | Soft and wet | Long and thin | Sharp and pointed
exercise: «Darwin's bark spider spins webs across rivers up to about 25 metres wide.» What does wide tell us here? | How heavy the web is | How many spiders live there | *How far the web reaches from one side to the other | How old the web is
test: «Lily was wide awake before the sun came up.» What does wide mean in «wide awake»? | *Fully awake | Covering many things | Far away | Very slow and tired
test: Sam says he has a wide choice of snacks. What does wide mean here? | Only one kind of snack | Snacks cut into wide slices | *Many different snacks to choose from | Snacks that are far away
exam: «Hammerhead sharks have wide heads with an eye at each end.» Which phrase means far and reaching across a large area? | *far and wide | wide open heads | sharks have | at each end
